WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.020
Li Lianjie is one of the most well known faces
in martial arts movies, but you probably know

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:10.080
him better as Jet Li . From martial arts movies
in the '80s and '90s up to modern-day franchises

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.110
like The Expendables, Li has been an action
star for as long as many moviegoers can remember.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:19.920
But fans were sent into a frenzy after a 2018
photo of the actor appearing aged beyond his

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.590
years went viral.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:25.650
The snapshot was almost unrecognizable as
the great martial arts star.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:30.420
Born in 1963, the martial artist would have
just turned 55 at the time the buzzworthy

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:35.070
picture was posted, but many thought he appeared
to be 20 or 30 years older.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:39.079
People made their concerns known all around
the world, but is there really any reason

00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:40.079
to worry?

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:43.470
Here are the real reasons why Jet Li looks
completely different now.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.760
Kung fu cult master

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.199
Jet Li is an actor with a rare résumé.

00:00:48.199 --> 00:00:53.260
Born in Beijing, Li grew up practicing martial
arts on a nationally competitive level, transitioning

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.499
to a movie career in his late teens.

00:00:55.499 --> 00:00:59.270
Since then, he's appeared in both Chinese
movies and Hollywood productions, but he slowed

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.780
down his Hollywood output around 2010.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:05.640
Li's partial withdrawal from the spotlight
had to do with a diagnosis of hyperthyroidism.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:10.000
When he announced he was suffering from the
illness, Li said that the condition left him

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.960
feeling uncertain as to whether or not he
could continue working as an actor in martial

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.190
arts movies.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:19.750
Despite this setback, Li seemed content about
the situation, saying in 2013,

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.880
"I'm in pain, but I'm not suffering.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.120
I'm happy."

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:34.760
Concerns gone viral

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:40.300
Li's diagnosis again became cause for concern
in May 2018 when a photo taken of him at a

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.180
Tibet temple went viral.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.470
The photo, which showed the five-foot-six
star hunched over, with short gray hair and

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.500
glasses, made him look remarkably older than
his age.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.420
Li's relative absence from American movie
screens in recent years, coupled with the

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:58.020
implied notion that he was gravely ill, helped
the image to circulate rapidly.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:03.381
Suddenly, a man who had convincingly defended
entire nations on the screen looked like the

00:02:03.381 --> 00:02:06.090
sort of person you would help to cross the
street.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:09.599
Fortunately, things aren't nearly as bad as
they might look.

00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:14.019
While an overactive thyroid can cause drastic
changes in one's weight and resting heart

00:02:14.019 --> 00:02:16.069
rate, it's a treatable condition.

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:20.489
While the disease has required Li to change
up his lifestyle, it's reportedly never threatened

00:02:20.489 --> 00:02:21.689
his life.

00:02:21.689 --> 00:02:23.650
As his manager told The Washington Post,

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:28.010
"He has hyperthyroidism that he's been dealing
with for almost 10 years.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:30.170
It's nothing life-threatening and he's dealing
with it.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:31.980
He’s all well and good."

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.540
A painful career

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:38.299
Li has a lot more going on with his body than
an overactive thyroid, and he's been building

00:02:38.299 --> 00:02:42.239
up the damage in plain sight, for our entertainment,
his whole life.

00:02:42.239 --> 00:02:47.209
As a result of his many injuries, Li has said
he suffers from problems in his legs and spine,

00:02:47.209 --> 00:02:50.670
with the issues keeping him from being able
to stand up straight for too long.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.790
The damage is part of a history in martial
arts that goes back decades, earning him a

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:59.141
torn knee that required surgery to fix at
the age of 18, and a major back injury by

00:02:59.141 --> 00:03:00.749
the age of 23.

00:03:00.749 --> 00:03:05.430
According to the South China Morning Post,
Li has said he was told by doctors in 2013

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:09.580
that he would end up in a wheelchair if he
continued to work in martial arts films, which

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.319
helps to account for his slowed output in
the genre since then.

00:03:12.319 --> 00:03:13.670
Who could blame him?

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:18.989
The movies he's already done get to live forever,
but Li himself only gets one chance.

00:03:18.989 --> 00:03:20.739
From a bad angle

00:03:20.739 --> 00:03:24.909
Li's public relations people were quick to
pounce on the emerging viral story, with his

00:03:24.909 --> 00:03:28.379
manager telling USA Today that his client
was "completely fine."

00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:33.510
Though Li's manager assured readers that Li
appreciated the outpouring of concern, he

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:37.590
also made it clear that the rumors of Li's
declining health were greatly exaggerated,

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:42.500
not to mention a snap judgment, based on one
photo of questionable composition.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.049
As Li's manager put it,

00:03:44.049 --> 00:03:47.239
"It's one picture and people are making these
interpretations from it.

00:03:47.239 --> 00:03:51.200
If you took a picture [of] me at the wrong
angle and wrong time of the day, I could look

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.890
frail as well."

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:56.609
As the photo gained traction with news outlets
around the world, social media commentators

00:03:56.609 --> 00:04:01.200
pointed out that much of Li's appearance could
come down to issues of lighting, posture,

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.139
and other external factors not indicative
of failing health.

00:04:04.139 --> 00:04:06.110
The bad photo theory has merit.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:10.870
In December 2017, Li shared a video on Instagram
wishing his fans a Happy New Year.

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:14.840
While his appearance in the video is similar
to his look in the viral photo, he appears

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:18.269
considerably healthier, older, but not in
trouble.

00:04:18.269 --> 00:04:20.650
"Dear fans, this is Jet!

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:26.090
I wish you happy holidays in the great year
2018."

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:27.440
Romeo is fine

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:32.270
While Li does look different now, it doesn't
appear to be because his health is declining,

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:35.770
nor are things as bad as one photo makes it
look.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:39.419
Li is still working as a filmmaker, though
he's kept most of his work aside from the

00:04:39.419 --> 00:04:41.360
Expendables series in China.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:45.500
That may change soon, as the actor is reportedly
in talks to star in the live-action version

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:48.530
of Disney's Mulan, set for release in 2020.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:52.479
Li may be getting older, but rumors of his
condition have been greatly exaggerated.

00:04:52.479 --> 00:04:56.460
Just because he's cooled it with the high
kicks doesn't mean he's done kicking around.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:57.470
Thanks for watching!

